<title>TURKEY: Turkish firm sells Algeria 25,000T flour at $305/T. [CORRECTED 15:55 GMT]</title>
<headline>Turkish firm sells Algeria 25,000T flour at $305/T. [CORRECTED 15:55 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects price in headline from $350/T)</p>
<p>Turkish private miller Uncular said on Friday it had begun selling 25,000 tonnes of wheat flour to Algeria's state company Enial at $305 per tonne.  </p>
<p>&quot;We have sent two batches of 5,500 and 3,650 tonnes and will complete the shipments in the next two months,&quot; said Cengiz Genc, an export official from Uncular.</p>
<p>He did not give other details.</p>
<p>--Ercan Ersoy, Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
